winex11: Render offscreen for a window of another process.

A client surface for a top-level window without children was rendered
onscreen: its client X window is meant to be attached to the window's whole
X window. Attaching needs the window's x11drv data, which only exists in
the process that owns the window. When another process renders to it, the
client window is created under the dummy parent and stays there, so what is
presented to it never reaches the screen.

Google Chrome draws every window from its GPU process. Its browser window
has child windows, so it is rendered offscreen and copied, and shows; its
bubbles ("Restore pages?", the profile and password bubbles) have none, and
stayed blank white: with WINEDEBUG=+dxgi, Chrome 156 presents 18 frames to
the profile bubble's swapchain, and +x11drv shows its client window created
without window data and never made offscreen. As the "Restore pages?"
bubble cannot be seen or closed, Chrome also keeps recording its exits as
crashes, by design, until the user acknowledges the crash.

Render offscreen when the window belongs to another process: the offscreen
path copies each frame to the window's whole X window, which works from any
process, as it does for Chrome's browser window. Tested on WinCraft 0.8.3
(Wine 11.19) with the patched winex11.so bind-mounted over the installed
one: Chrome's profile and "Restore pages?" bubbles are drawn with GPU
compositing, closing the latter makes Chrome record a clean exit again, and
the browser window is unchanged.

Status: not for WineHQ as it stands. This patch was written with an LLM,
and WineHQ does not accept LLM-generated code. No WineHQ bug describes
this yet (bugs.winehq.org searched for "chrome popup blank", "chromium
white popup" and "client window another process opengl" on 2026-10-25).
Upstream master has the same code.
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
@@ -222,8 +222,11 @@ static BOOL needs_client_window_clipping( HWND hwnd )
 
 static BOOL needs_offscreen_rendering( HWND hwnd, BOOL raw )
 {
+    DWORD pid;
+
     if (!raw && NtUserGetDpiForWindow( hwnd ) != NtUserGetWinMonitorDpi( hwnd, MDT_RAW_DPI )) return TRUE; /* needs DPI scaling */
     if (NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_PARENT ) != NtUserGetDesktopWindow()) return TRUE; /* child window, needs compositing */
+    if (NtUserGetWindowThread( hwnd, &pid ) && pid != GetCurrentProcessId()) return TRUE; /* other process window, client window cannot be attached */
     if (NtUserGetWindowRelative( hwnd, GW_CHILD )) return needs_client_window_clipping( hwnd ); /* window has children, needs compositing */
     return FALSE;
 }
